<title>UK: John Lewis UK store sales up 14.5% in week.</title>
<headline>John Lewis UK store sales up 14.5% in week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The John Lewis Partnership said its UK department store sales rose 14.5 percent in the week to January 11 compared with the same week a year earlier.</p>
<p>In the 24 weeks to January 11, sales were up 12.4 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>Total sales, including the Waitrose supermarket chain, rose 12.1 percent in the week and were up 10.7 percent in the 24-week period.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5109</p>
</text>
